# control-graph

When the task is a **multi-step agent cycle**, long autonomous run, model-routing choice, or risk of unbounded ReAct:

1. Read [control-graph/SKILL.md](../control-graph/SKILL.md) (formal SoT).
2. Expand [control-graph/references/english-procedure.md](../control-graph/references/english-procedure.md) **only if** the formal spec is ambiguous.
3. Open a **Control Card** (phase, budgets, inner DAG/subloop, current model role).
4. Prefer outer phases (ORIENT → PLAN → EXECUTE → VERIFY → REPAIR → REVIEW_GATE → INTEGRATE → DONE) over implicit “keep calling tools.”
5. Route **fast / explore / coding / deep / review** per the skill matrix; separate review from implementer context.
6. Honor HITL pause gates and hard exits (`max_loop_iters`, `no_progress`, cancel).

Compose with `agent-orchestrator` (triage + workers), `subagent-delegation` (explore), `fusion-sage` / `ai-optimization` (synthesis / prune). Do **not** put domain finder/CV/X logic here — only control-graph shape.

Activation: “control-graph”, “looper”, “structured loop”, “state machine”, “SM+DAG”, “model routing”, infinite-loop risk.
